  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oshkosh Defense has $477M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Oshkosh Defense has 3,993 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $119K and obligations down 67.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show variability: FY21 was $2.2B, FY22 was $1.6B, FY23 was $2B, FY24 was $1.3B, FY25 was $1.5B, and FY26 is $477M. The Department of Defense is the top buyer this year and obligated $477M. The General Services Administration also appears among buyers with $243 in recorded obligations. Truck Trailer Manufacturing is the largest market for Oshkosh Defense this year at $333M, followed by Hardware Manufacturing at $26.2M and Motor Vehicle Body Manufacturing at $21.4M. Other notable markets include Heavy Duty Truck Manufacturing at $19.6M and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing at $16.9M. Current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
