        "heading": "How did Oshkosh Defense perform this fiscal year compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 67.8% year over year to $477M in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year obligations by year were: FY21 $2.2B, FY22 $1.6B, FY23 $2B, FY24 $1.3B, FY25 $1.5B, and FY26 $477M. The Department of Defense is the top buying agency, accounting for $477M of obligations this year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Oshkosh Defense’s main products and markets to the federal government?",
        "body": "Truck Trailer Manufacturing is the largest market with $333M in obligations this year. Additional markets and their obligations include Hardware Manufacturing $26.2M, Motor Vehicle Body Manufacturing $21.4M, Heavy Duty Truck Manufacturing $19.6M, and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing $16.9M."
      }
